          "filename": "Anapji Pond-Gyeongju-Korea-2006-07.jpg",
          "caption": "A reconstructed pavilion at Anapji lake, a pleasure garden built after the kingdom of Silla unified most of the Korean Peninsula. Anapji, lake is located in Gyeongju National Park, South Korea.  Anapji, is an artificial pond located in Gyeongju National Park, South Korea. Gyeongju was the ancient capital of the Silla kingdom and the pond was constructed by order of King Munmu in 674 CE. Anapji is situated at the northeast edge of the Banwolseong palace site, in central Gyeongju. It contains three small islands.",
